cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MEMBRANE in academic or technical work, please cite this
  software using the metadata in this file.
title: >-
  MEMBRANE: A Local Model Runtime and Product Layer for llama.cpp
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Altıntaş
    given-names: Kadir Eren
repository-code: "https://github.com/kadireren7/membrane"
version: "0.8.0"
date-released: "2026-09-07"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  MEMBRANE is an open-source product/runtime layer built on top of
  llama.cpp: a built-in model catalog with real HTTPS download and
  checksum verification, hardware-aware variant selection, memory-aware
  KV-cache precision/residency planning (an --auto joint planner with
  bounded apply-time fallback), a persistent local background service
  with model-lifecycle management (`membrane use MODEL` -- select,
  consent-gated auto-install, and live model switching with no
  restart), and a real OpenAI-compatible chat API (streaming, stop
  sequences, bounded admission) validated against the official Python
  and Node.js `openai` SDKs. It does not reimplement llama.cpp's own
  inference engine -- it chooses, fits, installs, plans for, and serves
  models on top of it. CPU and Vulkan are validated on real local
  hardware; CUDA and Metal are each validated on one real device (see
  docs/support-matrix.md for the exact, current evidence-scoped
  matrix -- not a claim of universal hardware coverage). Windows and
  macOS are continuously validated on real GitHub-hosted CI runners
  (CPU-only on Windows; a paravirtualized Metal device on macOS); no
  official Windows/macOS package exists yet. An official Debian-family
  amd64 .deb package is available for Linux, installable and onboarded
  end to end with a single `membrane setup`/`membrane use MODEL`
  command (`membrane doctor` for diagnostics); independent multi-host
  validation beyond the maintainer's own development hardware and
  GitHub-hosted CI remains limited as of this release. This citation
  targets the latest stable release, v0.8.0; the repository's main
  branch may contain development changes beyond it. Archived
  experiments, negative results, and benchmark/FPGA/CXL simulation
  provenance live in the companion repository
  kadireren7/membrane-research.
keywords:
  - llama.cpp
  - LLM
  - KV cache
  - inference
  - memory management
  - Vulkan
  - CUDA
  - Metal
  - quantization
  - GPU offload
  - OpenAI-compatible API
  - local AI
